Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Ring: one Shared MTLBuffer of the capacity asked, the draw inputs'
span allocator with the wrap rule (a span past the tail jumps the
head to the start), the flush rule firing at half the ring walked
(the Vulkan twin's RING_SIZE/RING_FLUSH/IN_FLIGHT constants carried
one to one), and the spans retiring per their command buffer's
completion. the tests walk the exact cycle: climb, retire, wrap,
flush, and the overflow's honest refusal.

141 tests green; the ring is the foundation A4's draw execution rides
(the uniforms, the vertex uploads, and the texture staging all take
their spans here).
